0..60 Comment "// A Tarski universe closed under pairs and dependent pairs."
61..63 Comment "//"
64..142 Comment "// Martin-Löf\'s universe is closed under dependent functions, dependent pairs"
143..218 Comment "// and identity types. Each such code decodes to a family at the decodes of"
219..295 Comment "// its fields. A decode thus stands as a family\'s argument, a call in place."
296..331 Comment "// The call is the type it returns."
332..334 Comment "//"
335..411 Comment "// Each code is its own block. The pair code decodes to the pairs of its two"
412..483 Comment "// decodes. The dependent pair code decodes to the pairs over its first"
484..554 Comment "// decode. Its second field is a family of codes over that decode. The"
555..617 Comment "// decoder\'s binder takes the same decode, so the two convert."
618..620 Comment "//"
621..698 Comment "// - see: `pathological/universe/pair-and-path-codes.gandr` — a run for the"
699..744 Comment "//   first decode, and the path code, refused"
745..815 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/inductive-recursive.gandr` — the dependent"
816..840 Comment "//   functions, admitted"
841..911 Comment "// - see: Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_, Bibliopolis, 1984"
913..929 Comment "// The naturals."
